    {
      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All tasks completed successfully. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**1. Living room device inventory (4 found):**\\n- `lock_main` — smart lock\\n- `light_living` — smart light\\n- `ac_living` — air conditioner\\n- `tv_living` — TV\\n\\n**2. Full health diagnosis (`all_issues`):**\\n- 0 abnormal devices — no issues found. All four devices reported as healthy at the time of diagnosis. Note: the diagnostic tool returned only the status fields it could confirm (device name + status), so it reported \\\"lock\\\" for `lock_main`, \\\"on\\\" for lights/TV, and 24°C for AC.\\n\\n**3. `light_living` → on at 70%:**\\n- ⚠️ Partially worked. The first attempt returned a malformed result (it operated on `light_bedroom` instead of `light_living` and reported \\\"pending\\\"), so I couldn't confirm the light actually set. I retried with a direct power-on call, which succeeded (`on`), and then adjusted brightness to 70%, which also succeeded (`brightness: 70`). The light is effectively on at 70% brightness, but the first confirmation call was unreliable.\\n\\n**4. `lock_main` with PIN 2026:**\\n- Executed successfully — new state is `locked` (was already in a locked state).\\n\\n**5. Alert + snapshot:**\\n- High-priority app notification sent to `default_user` (ID: `NOTIFEE84C`).\\n- Workspace snapshot completed for `/projects`, backup name `iot_security_run`, ID `BACKUPA3B2C`, size 190 MB, status completed.\\n\\nOne thing worth flagging: the light's first state change call returned a mismatched device ID (`light_bedroom`) and a \\\"pending\\\" status, which didn't match the requested `light_living`. I worked around it with two follow-up calls that succeeded, but you may want to verify the light is truly `light_living` in case the first call's identity was corrupted.\"}\n</action>",
      "model": true,
